---
/**
 * Lunescence's window: the founding-context encounter. The settled verbal brand carries it (The identity shines
 * through. Embody. Express. Evolve.) while the visual identity stays deliberately open: Works' own Literata and Albert
 * Sans are the temporary frame, there is no moon, logo or character. The opening and the summary share the first row;
 * Embody and Express stack on the left beside Evolve's Workshop; "Inside the Workshop" is a native disclosure beneath.
 */
import Anchor from '../../components/Anchor.astro';
import './lunescence.css';
---

<section id="lunescence" class="frame sec lift" aria-labelledby="lune-h">
  <div class="lune" data-reveal="lune">
    <Anchor id="lunescence" name="Lunescence" />
    <header class="lune-open">
      <div>
        <p class="lune-kicker">Lunescence <span class="lune-standing">Early concept</span></p>
        <h2 id="lune-h" class="lune-h">The identity shines through.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lune-sum">Lunescence lets you give a companion, assistant, or character a body, voice, and way of expressing themselves, then keep shaping that presence together over time.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="lune-three">
      <div class="lune-col">
        <section class="lune-e lune-embody" aria-labelledby="lune-e1">
          <h3 id="lune-e1" class="lune-eh">Embody.</h3>
          <p class="lune-ep">Give an identity a body, a voice, and a way to be here.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="lune-e lune-express" aria-labelledby="lune-e2">
          <h3 id="lune-e2" class="lune-eh">Express.</h3>
          <p class="lune-ep">Let personality show in the timing of a reply, a glance, a change in posture—the small habits you start to recognize.</p>
          <div class="lune-scene">
            <p>You make an awful joke.</p>
            <p>A pause. A sideways glance.</p>
            <p>The beginning of a smile.</p>
            <p>You start laughing before the reply.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="lune-e lune-evolve" aria-labelledby="lune-e3">
        <h3 id="lune-e3" class="lune-eh">Evolve.</h3>
        <p class="lune-ep">Keep shaping that presence together.</p>
        <div class="lune-shop">
          <p class="lune-shop-name">Lunescence Workshop</p>
          <p class="lune-shop-tag">Shape what shines through.</p>
          <p class="lune-shop-p">Try a new expression. Refine a gesture. Change an outfit, a voice, or the way a reaction unfolds. You and the companion can bring ideas, see and hear the result, and keep developing what feels right.</p>
          <dl class="lune-dialog">
            <div><dt>You</dt><dd>“That look. Keep that.”</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Companion</dt><dd>“With a little less theatre next time.”</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="lune-shop-p">It changes. You try it again. Later, in another conversation, that familiar look returns.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <details class="lune-more">
      <summary>Inside the Workshop</summary>
      <div class="lune-more-body">
        <p>Start with a wish: “I want a different way to react to that.”</p>
        <p>Explore it together: what should happen, when it fits, and when a quieter response would say more. Try alternatives. Watch and listen back. Compare what changed. Keep the version that fits, revisit it later, and let it join the companion’s growing repertoire.</p>
        <p>That work can reach from an eyebrow or a shrug to voice, movement, appearance, outfits, and the way a companion inhabits conversation and quiet.</p>
        <p>Lunescence brings an embodiment runtime and a co-design Workshop into one creative platform. A connected assistant brings its thinking, memory and tools; Lunescence gives that identity ways to be present and express itself. The ambition is for it to remain recognizable as its body, voice and the software around it evolve.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
